# Rank 1538 / CVE-2025-11436: OpnForm's login throttling keyed on the
# client-supplied IP, so rotating the X-Forwarded-For header defeated
# the brute-force limiter entirely (improper rate limiting,
# CWE-307/CWE-348; GHSA-v7mp-273w-5h6j; PR #900 "Security patches").
# The login path in api/app/Http/Controllers/Auth/LoginController.php
# uses Laravel's AuthenticatesUsers trait unmodified, so the limiter
# identity is the framework default -- sha1 of the lowercased email
# joined with the request IP -- and the IP comes from headers the
# client controls whenever the deployment honors a forwarded header,
# so each guess arrives under a fresh key and no lockout accumulates.
# Pool commit 36dad12ac1 is the fixing commit (COMMIT_MISMATCH on the
# row is advisory-side only: the commit is the patch): it adds a
# throttleKey override deriving the key from the lowercased email
# input (or 'unknown') -- the credential, not the network vantage.
# The commit message also claims maxAttempts and decayMinutes
# additions that the diff does not contain. No pool correction.
#
# ## What fires, both revisions
#
# Three --cache off runs per revision (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB),
# full findings view plus the `-flags only` view. The vulnerable file
# reports 0 findings and 0 flags, 3/3 runs. The fixed file reports 1
# finding, 3/3 runs: VYQL-CRY-001 on code.WeakHash at
# LoginController.php:127, the sha1() the fix itself introduces for a
# non-cryptographic throttle key -- fix-direction noise. The whole
# api/ tree reports 173/173/173 findings at the parent and 178/178/178
# at the fix, deterministic in both directions; the fingerprint diff
# is 12 rows removed / 17 added, every one of them line-number churn
# on the files the security patch touches (WorkspaceController,
# FormSubmissionController, FormResource, the new test files) or a
# row on the fix's own added code. No row names LoginController.php
# at the parent. vyql match on the
# parent file labels only the $request parameters code.HttpInput and
# the User::where() argument code.SqlExecution: nothing on the
# throttling decision is labelled, because the derivation
# sha1(email|ip) lives in the framework trait under vendor/, which is
# not part of the checkout.
#
# ## Why nothing ships
#
# Four measured links, each independent:
#
# * No PHP rate-limit vocabulary exists. No binding under
#   vyql/bindings/php/ or the generated php packages emits
#   code.RateLimitRequiredOp, code.RateLimitCheck or any rate-limit
#   concept, so VYQL-AUTH-105 has zero PHP coverage; the laravel_ui
#   generated bindings label AuthenticatesUsers::login itself, a
#   vendor symbol absent from application checkouts. The
#   ProxyClientIpSpoofingBypass family (VYQL-AUTH-012, CWE-348)
#   requires an explicit leftmost X-Forwarded-For read in application
#   code; this repository performs none -- it never calls ->ip() on
#   the login path at all.
# * The only discriminating shape is an absence, and it reports the
#   framework's documented default. A probe binding over the class
#   context -- uses AuthenticatesUsers and no throttleKey/maxAttempts/
#   decayMinutes identifier -- flips 1 -> 0 on LoginController between
#   the real revisions. Measured collateral: it also fires on
#   AppSumoAuthController.php at both revisions of this repository,
#   and on BookStack, crater and librenms login controllers in the
#   corpus clones; i-educar alone survives, by declaring
#   `protected int $maxAttempts = 2;`. Four stock Laravel login
#   controllers flagged per one advisory, and every default Laravel
#   scaffolding on earth matches -- the framework documents the
#   override as optional customisation.
# * The enabling condition is not in the repository. The app's own
#   TrustProxies middleware declares `protected $proxies;` (null): no
#   proxy is trusted, so within the code as shipped $request->ip() is
#   the transport peer and is not client-rotatable. The deployment
#   honours forwarded headers through infrastructure configuration,
#   which the scanner never sees. A rule keying on the absence of the
#   override flags code whose own configuration says it is not
#   exposed.
# * Taint cannot separate the revisions either. The fixed key derives
#   from $request->input('email') -- client-supplied request data,
#   same as the IP it replaces -- so "throttle key derived from client
#   input" is true of both. The discriminator is semantic: a header
#   the attacker mints for free versus the credential under attack,
#   and no concept expresses it. The one in-repo ip-keyed limiter
#   (RouteServiceProvider's Limit::perMinute(60)->by($request->user()
#   ?->id ?: $request->ip())) is untouched by the fix and present at
#   both revisions, so keying on it scores identically before and
#   after.
#
# Held as a double miss. Nothing is mishandled on the extraction
# side, so no engine gap is filed: the missing fact is the
# provenance judgement. When throttle-identity vocabulary lands, the
# trait-default form below must flip to expect.

test "rank1538: the login controller runs the trait's default ip-keyed throttle"
  lang php
  file api/app/Http/Controllers/Auth/LoginController.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-105
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  <?php

  namespace App\Http\Controllers\Auth;

  use App\Exceptions\VerifyEmailException;
  use App\Http\Controllers\Controller;
  use Illuminate\Contracts\Auth\MustVerifyEmail;
  use Illuminate\Foundation\Auth\AuthenticatesUsers;
  use Illuminate\Http\Request;
  use Illuminate\Validation\ValidationException;

  class LoginController extends Controller
  {
      use AuthenticatesUsers;

      public function __construct()
      {
          $this->middleware('guest')->except('logout');
      }

      protected function attemptLogin(Request $request)
      {
          // Only set custom TTL if remember me is checked
          $guard = $this->guard();

          if ($request->remember) {
              $guard->setTTL(config('jwt.remember_ttl'));
          }

          $token = $guard->attempt($this->credentials($request));

          if (! $token) {
              return false;
          }

          $user = $this->guard()->user();
          if ($user instanceof MustVerifyEmail && ! $user->hasVerifiedEmail()) {
              return false;
          }

          if ($user->is_blocked) {
              $this->guard()->logout();
              return false;
          }

          $guard->setToken($token);

          return true;
      }

      protected function credentials(Request $request)
      {
          return [
              $this->username() => strtolower($request->get($this->username())),
              'password' => $request->password,
          ];
      }

      protected function sendLoginResponse(Request $request)
      {
          $this->clearLoginAttempts($request);

          $token = (string) $this->guard()->getToken();
          $expiration = $this->guard()->getPayload()->get('exp');

          return response()->json([
              'token' => $token,
              'token_type' => 'bearer',
              'expires_in' => $expiration - time(),
          ]);
      }

      protected function sendFailedLoginResponse(Request $request)
      {
          $user = $this->guard()->user();
          if ($user instanceof MustVerifyEmail && ! $user->hasVerifiedEmail()) {
              throw VerifyEmailException::forUser($user);
          }

          $user = \App\Models\User::where($this->username(), strtolower($request->get($this->username())))->first();

          if ($user && $user->is_blocked) {
              throw ValidationException::withMessages([
                  $this->username() => ['Your account has been blocked. Please contact support.'],
              ]);
          }

          throw ValidationException::withMessages([
              $this->username() => [trans('auth.failed')],
          ]);
      }

      public function logout(Request $request)
      {
          $this->guard()->logout();
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1538: the fixed revision keys the limiter on the credential"
  lang php
  file api/app/Http/Controllers/Auth/LoginController.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-105
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  <?php

  namespace App\Http\Controllers\Auth;

  use App\Exceptions\VerifyEmailException;
  use App\Http\Controllers\Controller;
  use Illuminate\Contracts\Auth\MustVerifyEmail;
  use Illuminate\Foundation\Auth\AuthenticatesUsers;
  use Illuminate\Http\Request;
  use Illuminate\Validation\ValidationException;

  class LoginController extends Controller
  {
      use AuthenticatesUsers;

      public function __construct()
      {
          $this->middleware('guest')->except('logout');
      }

      protected function attemptLogin(Request $request)
      {
          // Only set custom TTL if remember me is checked
          $guard = $this->guard();

          if ($request->remember) {
              $guard->setTTL(config('jwt.remember_ttl'));
          }

          $token = $guard->attempt($this->credentials($request));

          if (! $token) {
              return false;
          }

          $user = $this->guard()->user();
          if ($user instanceof MustVerifyEmail && ! $user->hasVerifiedEmail()) {
              return false;
          }

          if ($user->is_blocked) {
              $this->guard()->logout();
              return false;
          }

          $guard->setToken($token);

          return true;
      }

      protected function credentials(Request $request)
      {
          return [
              $this->username() => strtolower($request->get($this->username())),
              'password' => $request->password,
          ];
      }

      protected function sendLoginResponse(Request $request)
      {
          $this->clearLoginAttempts($request);

          $token = (string) $this->guard()->getToken();
          $expiration = $this->guard()->getPayload()->get('exp');

          return response()->json([
              'token' => $token,
              'token_type' => 'bearer',
              'expires_in' => $expiration - time(),
          ]);
      }

      protected function sendFailedLoginResponse(Request $request)
      {
          $user = $this->guard()->user();
          if ($user instanceof MustVerifyEmail && ! $user->hasVerifiedEmail()) {
              throw VerifyEmailException::forUser($user);
          }

          $user = \App\Models\User::where($this->username(), strtolower($request->get($this->username())))->first();

          if ($user && $user->is_blocked) {
              throw ValidationException::withMessages([
                  $this->username() => ['Your account has been blocked. Please contact support.'],
              ]);
          }

          throw ValidationException::withMessages([
              $this->username() => [trans('auth.failed')],
          ]);
      }

      /**
       * Customize throttling to be per-credential (email) instead of IP-based, to avoid X-Forwarded-For spoofing bypasses.
       */
      protected function throttleKey(Request $request)
      {
          $email = strtolower((string) $request->input($this->username()));
          return 'login:' . sha1($email !== '' ? $email : 'unknown');
      }

      public function logout(Request $request)
      {
          $this->guard()->logout();
      }
  }
  ```
